{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "radiation-protection",
    "title": "Radiation Protection",
    "order": 9
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "facility-safety-systems",
    "title": "Facility Safety Systems",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Controlling Exposure at the Facility Level",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Personal dosimeters tell you how much dose someone received \u2014 but a facility also needs physical and procedural systems that prevent unnecessary exposure from happening in the first place. This lesson covers area classification, warning systems, interlocks, and shielding design."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Controlled vs. Uncontrolled Areas",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Area type"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Definition"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Dose limit"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Controlled area",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Access is controlled specifically for radiation protection; must be clearly marked"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "1 mSv/week (50 mSv/year)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Uncontrolled area",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Individuals present aren't monitored by a radiation safety program"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "0.1 mSv/week (5 mSv/year)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Notice the uncontrolled area limit is 1/10th of the controlled area limit \u2014 the same public-vs-occupational ratio that shows up throughout radiation protection."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A hospital hallway adjacent to a treatment vault, where members of the public may walk without radiation monitoring, is best classified as:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "A controlled area",
              "An uncontrolled area"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Since the people present aren't monitored by a radiation safety program, this space is classified \u2014 and dose-limited \u2014 as uncontrolled."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Warning Signs and Lights",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Entrances to treatment rooms must be clearly marked with signs warning of potential radiation presence."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Important distinction:",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " warning lights (at the control panel, room entrance, and on the treatment machine) indicate the machine is "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "turned on",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 they do "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "not",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " necessarily indicate radiation is actually being produced at that instant. Don't confuse \"machine powered on\" with \"beam on.\""
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Door Interlocks",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Treatment room entrances are engineered so that opening the door automatically turns off the machine or returns a source to a safe shielded position. This is a hard physical safety mechanism, not just a procedural rule \u2014 it functions even if a therapist forgets a step."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Staying Connected to the Patient",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Because the therapist must leave the room during beam-on, maintaining both visual and auditory contact with the patient is essential \u2014 typically via closed-circuit TV and a two-way intercom. This isn't just about patient comfort; it's how a therapist would immediately notice a medical emergency or a patient movement problem during treatment."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Emergency Off Controls",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Emergency off buttons immediately remove electrical power from the treatment machine. They're placed in multiple locations for a reason \u2014 treatment room walls, on the treatment couch itself, near the exit, and at the control panel \u2014 so that whoever needs to stop the machine, wherever they are in the room, can reach one quickly."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page6_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Why are emergency off controls placed in multiple locations throughout the treatment room?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "So whoever needs to stop the machine can reach a control quickly regardless of where they're standing",
              "It's simply a regulatory formality with no practical purpose"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Multiple emergency-off locations exist so that in an actual emergency, someone doesn't have to cross the room to reach a single control."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Mazes and Shielding Construction",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Treatment rooms are physically built to prevent radiation leakage and scattered radiation from escaping a high-dose area:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Mazes",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 bent hallway entrances that force scattered radiation to bounce multiple times (losing energy each time) before it could reach an open doorway, instead of a straight shot out"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Doors",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 lead-lined, often around 7 inches thick, and can weigh up to 4,200 lbs"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Walls",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 thick concrete construction, engineered based on the beam energy the room is designed for"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This is why treatment vaults can't simply be relocated within a building without significant construction \u2014 the room itself is part of the radiation safety system."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered controlled vs. uncontrolled area classification, warning signs and lights, door interlocks, patient communication systems, emergency off controls, and maze/shielding construction."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Together with Personnel Monitoring & Dosimetry and ALARA, this completes the core radiation protection picture: how much dose is tracked, how it's limited by policy, and how the facility itself is physically built to control it."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
